### 4.2 Deterministic Domain Engines (`backend/app/engines/`)

1. **`cs_repo_engine.py` (Real Dependency, AST & Sandbox Evaluator):**
   - **Pre-loaded Demo 1:** Evaluates `lodash@4.17.20` (`CVE-2021-23337` Command Injection in `_.template` & `CVE-2020-8203` Prototype Pollution).
   - **Live Custom Repo / `package.json` Mode:**
     - Parses any uploaded `package.json` or fetches `raw.githubusercontent.com/{owner}/{repo}/HEAD/package.json` (with offline fallback parser if no internet).
     - Scans dependencies against an embedded curated CVE advisory dictionary (`lodash`, `express`, `axios`, `jsonwebtoken`, `mongoose`, `webpack`, `minimist`, `semver`, `ws`, `tar`, `fastapi`, `pydantic`, `requests`, `flask`, `django`) + live OSV.dev API lookup when online.
     - Computes the **PatchPath Cost Function** for each candidate plan:
       $$\text{Cost}(P) = 50 \cdot (\text{RemainingCVEs}) + 40 \cdot (\text{BrokenTestsOrASTCallSites}) + 25 \cdot \left(\frac{\text{ChangedPackages}}{\text{TotalPackages}}\right) - 15 \cdot (\text{TestEvidenceConfidence})$$

2. **`ece_circuit_engine.py` (Real Nodal Thermal & LDO ESR Stability Solver):**
   - Computes real physics equations for a 5V IoT Sensor Board (`V_in = 12.0V`, `V_out = 5.0V`, `I_load = 0.35A`, `T_ambient = 30.0°C`):
     - Power dissipation: $P_D = (V_{in} - V_{out}) \cdot I_{load} = (12 - 5) \times 0.35 = 2.45\text{ W}$.
     - **Initial State (`LM7805` without large heatsink, $R_{\theta JA} = 36^\circ\text{C/W}$):**
       $$T_J = 30 + (2.45 \times 36) = 118.2^\circ\text{C} \quad (\text{CRITICAL THERMAL OVERLOAD} > 85^\circ\text{C target})$$
     - **Plan A (`AMS1117-5.0` Naive Swap with existing $0.015\Omega$ MLCC ceramic cap):**
       - `AMS1117` stability requires $0.4\Omega \le \text{ESR} \le 5.0\Omega$. Because $0.015\Omega < 0.4\Omega$, loop phase margin drops below $10^\circ$, causing `420 mVpp` sub-harmonic oscillation (`FAILURE_CODE: ESR_PHASE_MARGIN_INSTABILITY`).
     - **Plan B (`PatchPath Minimal Validated Fix`: High-Efficiency Buck/LDO module `MCP1702 / TSR-1-2450` + matched $1\mu\text{F}$ ceramic cap):**
       - Stabilizes phase margin ($68^\circ$), drops $T_J$ to $41.2^\circ\text{C}$, keeps ripple at $4.0\text{ mVpp}$, and modifies only `2` component pads (`Blast Radius: 14%`).

3. **`civil_truss_engine.py` (Real NumPy 2D/3D Truss Stiffness Matrix Solver):**
   - Uses `numpy` to compute member axial forces, stresses $\sigma = F / A$, and Euler buckling ratios $\text{BR} = |F_{\text{comp}}| / P_{cr}$ where $P_{cr} = \frac{\pi^2 E I}{(K L)^2}$:
     - **Initial State:** Member `B4-C4` under `180 kN` peak deck load has $\text{BR} = 1.14 > 1.0$ (`STRUCTURAL_BUCKLING_RISK`).
     - **Plan A (Naive Solid Steel Beam Swap):** Increases dead weight at Joint `C4` by `+340 kg`, driving gusset bolt shear stress at `C4` to `310 MPa > 250 MPa yield` (`FAILURE_CODE: ADJACENT_JOINT_SHEAR_OVERLOAD`).
     - **Plan B (PatchPath Minimal Fix — Hollow Structural Section `HSS 100x100x6` + local stiffening gusset):** Drops buckling ratio to `0.55` (`Safety Factor: 1.82`), adds only `+18 kg` dead weight, and keeps all adjacent joints within safe limits (`Blast Radius: 11%`).

4. **`upskiller_engine.py` (The Universal Idea & Project Upskiller Engine):**
